{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Sky Augmentation versus Extraction.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Sky Augmentation versus Extraction.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"sky augmentation versus extraction sky augmentation versus extraction","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Sky Augmentation versus Extraction.md","fileName":"Sky Augmentation versus Extraction.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Sky Augmentation versus Extraction","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:17\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Matte Painting and Scene Finishing]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Matte Painting and Scene Finishing","Feathering a Composite Edge","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Sky Augmentation versus Extraction.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Sky Augmentation versus Extraction.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"sky augmentation versus extraction sky augmentation versus extraction","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Sky Augmentation versus Extraction.md","fileName":"Sky Augmentation versus Extraction.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Sky Augmentation versus Extraction","heading":"Sky Augmentation versus Extraction","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A flat, nearly uniform sky may be improved by laying a new sky plate over it and masking that plate just above the horizon, rather than extracting every foreground boundary. Edge feather and reduced opacity let the two skies blend. A more complex sky or horizon demands roto, paint, or a procedural extraction to separate scene elements. In either case, the new sky's sun direction and atmospheric color must agree with the ground plate; the book flips a cloud plate when its light direction conflicts with shadows. See [[Feathering a Composite Edge]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Matte Painting and Scene Finishing","Feathering a Composite Edge","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Sky Augmentation versus Extraction.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Sky Augmentation versus Extraction.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"sky augmentation versus extraction sky augmentation versus extraction","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Sky Augmentation versus Extraction.md","fileName":"Sky Augmentation versus Extraction.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Sky Augmentation versus Extraction","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Matte Painting and Scene Finishing","Feathering a Composite Edge","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}